s Animal Ethics Committee, which oversees the ethical use of animals in research and teaching in compliance with national codes and legislation. This role involves reviewing research proposals, attending monthly meetings, participating in facility inspections, and ensuring animal welfare is prioritised, with appropriate training, support, and reimbursement provided. More details... Indigenous Employment Program- Expression of Interest Indigenous Australian candidates; register your Expression of Interest here to receive regular job vacancy information at La Trobe University. More details... Current Opportunities Job Closes Research Fellow 6 Sep 2026 Help shape the future of HIV care! Join our pilot project co-designing a new model to integrate PozQoL across clinical, community and peer services. Powered by PageUp To perform a job search, select your preferred job criteria below. Job search Work Type Fixed Term 1 Location Australia Melbourne (Bundoora) 1 Category Academic Research 1 Classification Level - Academic Level B - Research Only 1 Want to know more? Recruitment contacts T: +61 (0)3 9479 1234 F: +61 (0)3 9471 0369 Jobs for students Jobs for staff [Restricted] Facebook Twitter Youtube Linked in Instagram Emergency information Contacts Site map Accessibility Privacy Copyright and disclaimer © Copyright 2014 La Trobe University. All rights reserved. CRICOS Provider Code: VIC 00115M"
